The action bar sits above your hotbar and replaces Iron’s native spell bar and mana overlay so the two do not stack.

What the HUD shows:

- Spell icons with cooldown overlays
- Affordability tinting when you cannot pay mana
- Compact keybind labels (for example `Q`, `s1`, `cR`)
- A mana bar styled for this actionbar

Cast with Iron’s quick-cast keys. The label on each slot is the key currently bound in Minecraft’s controls.

Companion HUD editors can preview and persist offsets through the Actionbar HUD APIs. If a slot looks empty, you have no spell equipped there — the bar stays quiet until at least one spell is set (especially when Codex is hiding the HUD until the first equip).
